  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on skewness, particularly favoring more right-skewed lotteries (those with higher concentration of probability on unfavorable outcomes). Lottery B is more right-skewed than A (75% on 0 vs. 50% on 0), so the reason would prefer B. However, the individual chose A and justified this based on the higher chance (50% vs. 25%) of winning something—i.e., avoiding zero. This reasoning moves in the opposite direction: avoiding unfavorable outcomes (zero) rather than accepting or preferring them, which contradicts the definition of favoring right-skewness. The individual considered probabilities of non-zero outcomes, not the overall skew of the distribution. There is no mention or implication of evaluating the shape of the outcome distribution. Therefore, the individual’s reasoning is inconsistent with the decision reason. The information considered and the justification are unrelated to skewness as defined.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

